     "<div class=\"gmail_extra\"><div class=\"gmail_quote\"><blockquote class=\"gmail_quote\" style=\"margin:0 0 0 .8ex;border-left:1px #ccc solid;padding-left:1ex\"><div dir=\"ltr\">I&#39;m using ggtree in an R kernel in Jupyter Notebook, and I&#39;m having trouble trying to change the plot size with certain tree layouts. The usual method for changing plot sizes in an R kernel is with:<div style=\"background-color:rgb(250,250,250);border-color:rgb(187,187,187);border-style:solid;border-width:1px;word-wrap:break-word\"><code><div><font color=\"#000000\"><span style=\"color:#000\">options</span><span style=\"color:#660\">(</span><span style=\"color:#000\">repr</span><span style=\"color:#660\">.</span><span style=\"color:#000\">plot</span><span style=\"color:#660\">.</span><span style=\"color:#000\">height</span><span style=\"color:#660\">=</span><span style=\"color:#066\">5</span><span style=\"color:#660\">,</span><span style=\"color:#000\"> repr</span><span style=\"color:#660\">.</span><span style=\"color:#000\">plot</span><span style=\"color:#660\">.</span><span style=\"color:#000\">width</span><span style=\"color:#660\">=</span><span style=\"color:#066\">6</span><span style=\"color:#660\">)</span></font><span style=\"color:#000\"><br></span></div></code></div><br>However, this does not change the tree size in most layouts (eg.,  &quot;circular&quot; or &quot;fan&quot;). Instead, the plot margins get bigger, while the actual tree stays the same size.  Is there a way to adjust the tree size in when displaying it in a Jupyter Notebook?</div></blockquote></div></div>"
